---
import '@/styles/globals.css';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Footer from '@/components/Footer.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Content from '@/components/Content.astro';
import {Separator} from '@/components/ui/separator';
import Code from '@/components/Code';
import { Card, CardHeader, CardTitle, CardDescription, CardContent, CardFooter } from "@/components/ui/card";
---

<Layout title="Tunnl.app — Get started">
    <Navbar animate={false}/>
    <main class='flex flex-col min-h-screen'>
        <Content>
            <div class='flex flex-col items-center mt-24 p-4'>
                <div class='w-full max-w-xl flex flex-col gap-4 text-lg'>
                    <h1 class='text-5xl font-semibold mb-3'>Quickstart guide</h1>
                    <h2 class='text-3xl font-semibold'>Setup your VPS</h2>
                    <Separator/>
                    <ol class='list-decimal space-y-6 ml-5'>
                        <li>
                            <div class='flex flex-col gap-2'>
                                <p>
                                    Pick up a cheap VPS with a public IPv4 or IPv6 address, 
                                    personally I use a Ubuntu 24.04 Hetzner VPS but you can
                                    use any provider. 
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    Just remember, 
                                    <strong>the VPS should be as close as possible to you</strong>.
                                    This is because your VPS will host your first OpenZiti Edge Router,
                                    which will be the entrypoint into your network.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Setup your user, add your ssh key to the VPS, and allow 
                            port 22/TCP through the firewall for ssh.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Install <Code>docker</Code>, <Code>openssl</Code>, 
                            and <Code>jq</Code> on your VPS.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Make sure you have a domain you can control.
                            I recommend Cloudflare if you want to buy one. To get a free domain
                            use DuckDNS.
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                    <h2 class='text-3xl font-semibold mt-6'>Install the Tunnl.app dashboard</h2>
                    <Separator/>
                    <ol class='list-decimal space-y-6 ml-5'>
                        <li>
                            <div class='flex flex-col gap-3'>
                                <p>
                                    Before you run the install script you need to configure 
                                    DNS for the dashboard, publisher, ziti controller, ziti router,
                                    and keycloak services.
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    Generally your DNS should look like this.
                                </p>
                                <Code className='p-2'>
                                    <ul class='list-none ml-5 space-y-1'>
                                        <li>ROOT_DOMAIN &rarr; A : VPS IP</li>
                                        <li>publisher.ROOT_DOMAIN &rarr; CNAME : ROOT_DOMAIN</li>
                                        <li>auth.ROOT_DOMAIN &rarr; CNAME : ROOT_DOMAIN</li>
                                        <li>ziti.ROOT_DOMAIN &rarr; CNAME : ROOT_DOMAIN</li>
                                        <li>*.ziti.ROOT_DOMAIN &rarr; CNAME : ziti.ROOT_DOMAIN</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </Code>
                                <p>
                                    If you want to put the Tunnl.app dashboard on a different subdomain
                                    than ROOT_DOMAIN which you will specify during the install, add this entry.
                                </p>
                                <Code className='p-2'>
                                    SUB_DOMAIN.ROOT_DOMAIN &rarr; CNAME : ROOT_DOMAIN
                                </Code>
                                <p>
                                    <strong>OR</strong> if you want a super easy DNS configuration 
                                    (may cause issues if you want letsencrypt certificates for ziti services
                                    later), add this to your DNS configuration.
                                </p>
                                <Code className='p-2'>
                                    <ul class='list-none ml-5 space-y-1'>
                                        <li>ROOT_DOMAIN &rarr; A : VPS IP</li>
                                        <li>*.ROOT_DOMAIN &rarr; CNAME : ROOT_DOMAIN</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </Code>
                                <p>
                                    To get the IP of your VPS run <Code className='w-fit'>curl -4 ifconfig.io</Code>.
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    My preferred way to get certificates for my web services 
                                    is with the Cloudflare DNS proxy. Another way is to use
                                    Traefik with a API key and configure a certResolver. 
                                    You could also manage the certificates externally yourself.
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    If you're using Cloudflare proxy DNS protect the ROOT_DOMAIN, publisher, and auth
                                    with proxy DNS. If you plan to put the dashboar on a subdomain of ROOT_DOMAIN,
                                    protect that subdomain too. Everything else only needs to resolve to your VPS.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Run these commands and make sure they all resolve to your VPS.
                            <div class='grid grid-cols-1 gap-3'>
                                <Code className='p-1 w-fit'>dig ROOT_DOMAIN</Code>
                                <Code className='p-1 w-fit'>dig auth.ROOT_DOMAIN</Code>
                                <Code className='p-1 w-fit'>dig publisher.ROOT_DOMAIN</Code>
                                <Code className='p-1 w-fit'>dig ziti.ROOT_DOMAIN</Code>
                                <Code className='p-1 w-fit'>dig ctrl.ziti.ROOT_DOMAIN</Code>
                                <Code className='p-1 w-fit'>dig er1.ziti.ROOT_DOMAIN</Code>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <div class='flex flex-col gap-2'>
                                <p>
                                    Run the quickstart script.
                                </p>
                                <Code className='my-1 p-1'>
                                    curl -sL tunnl.app/install.sh | sh
                                </Code>
                                <p>
                                    This with automatically setup a Ziti network with an edge router and controller,
                                    configure a keycloak realm for OIDC, and deploy the Tunnl.app dashboard
                                    along with the publisher service.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Go into the target directory and run <Code>docker compose up -d</Code> 
                            to deploy the Tunnl.app quickstart stack.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Test if the dashboard works by going to https://ROOT_DOMAIN,
                            or https://SUB_DOMAIN.ROOT_DOMAIN if you configured it that way.
                            Sign in enroll an idenity, and create a service!
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                </div> 
            </div>
        </Content>
        <div class='justify-end pt-10'>
            <Footer />
        </div>
    </main>
</Layout>

